[2026-01-30T15:29:45.616Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Execute this requirement immediately without asking questions.\n\n## REQUIREMENT\n\n# Each View Is An Intelligence Analyst Role\n\n## Metadata\n- **Category**: functionality\n- **Effort**: Unknown (N/A/3)\n- **Impact**: Unknown (N/A/3)\n- **Scan Type**: insight_synth\n- **Generated**: 1/30/2026, 1:25:21 AM\n\n## Description\nOverviewView is the executive summary, FindingsView is the evidence analyst, SourcesView is the source evaluator, AnalysisView is the contradiction detector, EntitiesView is the network mapper, PerspectivesView is the domain expert. Make these roles explicit: each view could have a persona with preferences.\n\n## Reasoning\nThe views implicitly model different analyst roles but this is not leveraged. Explicit personas could guide UX (what would a source evaluator want to see first?), enable role-based report generation, and create a mental model for users to understand what each view offers.\n\n## Context\n\n**Note**: This section provides supporting architectural documentation and is NOT a hard requirement. Use it as guidance to understand existing code structure and maintain consistency.\n\n### Context: Report Views\n\n**Description**: Full-page report views for different sections: overview, findings, sources, analysis, entities, and perspectives. Each view provides deep-dive content for its domain.\n**Related Files**:\n- `src/components/report/views/OverviewView.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/views/FindingsView.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/views/SourcesView.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/views/AnalysisView.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/views/EntitiesView.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/views/PerspectivesView.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/views/index.tsx`\n\n**Post-Implementation**: After completing this requirement, evaluate if the context description or file paths need updates. Use the appropriate API/DB query to update the context if architectural changes were made.\n\n## Recommended Skills\n\nUse Claude Code skills as appropriate for implementation guidance. Check `.claude/skills/` directory for available skills.\n\n## Notes\n\nThis requirement was generated from an AI-evaluated project idea. No specific goal is associated with this idea.\n\n## AFTER IMPLEMENTATION\n\n1. Log your implementation using the `log_implementation` MCP tool with:\n   - requirementName: the requirement filename (without .md)\n   - title: 2-6 word summary\n   - overview: 1-2 paragraphs describing what was done\n\n2. Check for test scenario using `check_test_scenario` MCP tool\n   - If hasScenario is true, call `capture_screenshot` tool\n   - If hasScenario is false, skip screenshot\n\n3. Verify: `npx tsc --noEmit` (fix any type errors)\n\nBegin implementation now."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"063d9692-0974-4418-8890-3933b0ef315a","uuid":"6f347fd9-fbb4-4b4c-a56f-0f3dc8c324aa","isSynthetic":true}
